35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The bay is capped at four hundred kilos. Last season, four call-outs roped it off during opening hours. The building is already struggling.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The data is clear. Head counts rise where mechanisms run, and comment slips name presence, not objects. We must fund the living gallery, not the static case.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,One person for two hundred pieces! That’s impossible. And the volunteers are already busy with walks. Who is actually left to set up the exhibition?,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, two out of four openings slipped! That’s scary. Plus, transport costs are huge. We need to pick something that actually arrives on time!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The joiner’s rate doubled, and bespoke mounts cost per object. Anything self-supporting saves us that bleed. I’ll stick with my two choices to map the true cost.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, mechanisms are heavy. If the bay is already capped, adding moving parts risks another closure. We must respect the floor’s limit.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, the bay’s limit is a constraint, not a verdict. The audience returns for presence, not weight. We must find a living exhibition that respects the structure.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Daisuke, you’re right! If the bay is capped, we can’t risk it. But with only one conservator, we can’t handle fragile items either. We need something sturdy and simple!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, exactly! If the paperwork is late, the crates are late. We need a local loan with simple, sturdy items. No fragile stuff that needs special handling!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, precisely. Local loans bypass the transport hemorrhage. We need self-supporting objects to avoid the bespoke mount trap. The invoices demand simplicity.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Benjamin, I agree. Self-supporting objects are safer for the floor. But we must also ensure the powered displays don’t trigger another closure.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, simplicity is necessary, but presence is the driver. We need a living exhibition that is self-supporting and respects the bay’s limit.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, presence is great, but who stands there? With one conservator and busy volunteers, we need a show that doesn’t need constant fixing!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, I agree! Simple, sturdy items mean fewer trips to the lab. Let’s pick a local loan so the paperwork doesn’t mess up the schedule again!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, exactly. Powered displays trigger those call-outs. We need static, self-supporting objects. No moving parts, no bespoke mounts. The budget demands stillness.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I’m glad we’re aligning. The floor cannot take more risk. I’ll stick with my findings to ensure the space remains safe and functional.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
